  <page_number>72</page_number>
  <running_head>I. IACOMOTI</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <catchword>Et</catchword>
    <signature></signature>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <p><i>Humanas elegis folicitudines,</i></p>
    <p><i>Et vitæ fragilis præcipites fugas</i></p>
    <p><i>Decantat querulo carmine clarior.</i></p>
    <p><i>Illi Musa dedit pungere acumine</i></p>
    <p><i>Mordaci vitium pectoribus latens,</i></p>
    <p><i>Argutisque iocis &amp; sale carpere</i></p>
    <p><i>Corruptos hominum praua sequentium</i></p>
    <p><i>Mores, atque vagæ damna licentiæ.</i></p>
    <p><i>Et si quem placido lumine respicit</i></p>
    <p><i>Phœbus, dat Cithara nectareum decus</i></p>
    <p><i>Blandæ: qua cecinit Stesichorus grauis,</i></p>
    <p><i>Alcaúsque minax, &amp; Rhodopeius</i></p>
    <p><i>Orpheus: quam facili pollice Anacreon</i></p>
    <p><i>Pulsauit teneris fœdus amoribus.</i></p>
    <p><i>Olim quam Latiis attulit auribus.</i></p>
    <p><i>Princeps Æolium carmen ad Italos</i></p>
    <p><i>Deduxisse modos Flaccus amabilis.</i></p>
    <p><i>Sunt qui Graiugenis carmina vocibus</i></p>
    <p><i>Scribunt: ast aliy Romulidas sonis</i></p>
    <p><i>Mulcent Ausonijs: Musáque vatibus</i></p>
    <p><i>Gallis dat patria ludere tibia:</i></p>
    <p><i>Paucis illa simul dona benigniór</i></p>
    <p><i>Mittit, si Charites tergeminæ fauent,</i></p>
    <p><i>Et Phœbus Cithara si pater annuit.</i></p>
    <p><i>Sic Bezam triplices ferre suum iubet</i></p>
    <p><i>Lauros, sic variis ornat honoribus</i></p>
    <p><i>Doctum Cecropio psallere pectine:</i></p>
    <p><i>Doctum Romuleo pangere barbito.</i></p>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Faint show-through from the facing page at the right margin is not transcribed. The catchword "Et" is at the lower right. Some words in the italic verse are uncertain: "Stesichorus", "Bezam" and "Ausonijs" are read as printed.</notes>
